---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FontTool from '../components/FontTool.astro';
import FaqSection from '../components/FaqSection.astro';
import SchemaOrg from '../components/SchemaOrg.astro';
import { t, getPath } from '../i18n';

const lang = 'en';
const strings = t(lang);

const siteUrl = Astro.site?.toString().replace(/\/$/, '') ?? '';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const pageUrl = siteUrl + getPath(lang, '/');
const logoUrl = `${siteUrl}${base}logo.svg`;
---

<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title={`${strings.site.name} — ${strings.site.tagline}`}
  description={strings.tool.subheading}
  path="/"
>
  <FontTool lang={lang} />

<article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 text-gray-800 leading-7">

  <header class="mb-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 mb-4">
      Font Generator – Create Fancy Fonts and Copy & Paste Stylish Text
    </h1>

    <p class="text-lg text-gray-600">
      A font generator makes it easy to turn normal text into stylish,
      fancy, and creative text that you can copy and paste into social
      media profiles, usernames, messages, and more.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
      What Is a Font Generator?
    </h2>

    <p class="mb-4">
      A font generator is an online tool that converts ordinary text into
      different font styles. Instead of installing a font file or using
      complicated design software, you can type your text and instantly
      explore different styles.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4">
      Many online font generators use Unicode characters to create styles
      such as bold, italic, cursive, gothic, monospace, bubble, and other
      decorative text. Because the result is text rather than an image,
      you can often copy and paste it into supported apps and websites.
    </p>

    <p>
      Try our
      <a
        href="/"
        class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline font-medium"
      >
        Font Generator
      </a>
      to create stylish text instantly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
      How Does a Font Generator Work?
    </h2>

    <p class="mb-4">
      Using a font generator is simple. You enter your normal text into
      the generator, and the tool creates multiple font styles from the
      same text. You can then preview the results and copy the style you
      like.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
      1. Enter Your Text
    </h3>

    <p class="mb-5">
      Start by typing a name, word, sentence, username, or social media
      bio into the text box. The generator can transform your text into
      several different styles.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
      2. Choose a Font Style
    </h3>

    <p class="mb-5">
      Browse the available styles and find one that matches your purpose.
      You may find bold, italic, script, gothic, bubble, monospace,
      aesthetic, and other fancy text styles.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
      3. Copy and Paste
    </h3>

    <p>
      Once you find a style you like, copy the generated text and paste
      it into your preferred app or website. This makes a font generator
      useful for creating usernames, bios, captions, messages, and other
      types of online text.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
      Popular Font Styles
    </h2>

    <p class="mb-5">
      Different font styles can give the same words a completely different
      appearance. Here are some popular styles people use with online font
      generators:
    </p>

    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-5">
      <li><strong>Bold fonts</strong> for strong and noticeable text.</li>
      <li><strong>Italic fonts</strong> for a softer or elegant look.</li>
      <li><strong>Cursive fonts</strong> for decorative and handwritten-style text.</li>
      <li><strong>Gothic fonts</strong> for dark and traditional designs.</li>
      <li><strong>Bubble fonts</strong> for playful usernames and posts.</li>
      <li><strong>Monospace fonts</strong> for a typewriter-style appearance.</li>
      <li><strong>Small caps</strong> for compact and distinctive text.</li>
      <li><strong>Decorative fonts</strong> for creative social media content.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      You can experiment with different
      <a
        href="/"
        class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline font-medium"
      >
        font styles
      </a>
      and choose the one that fits your text best.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
      Where Can You Use Fancy Fonts?
    </h2>

    <p class="mb-4">
      Fancy text can be useful in many places where Unicode text is
      supported. Creators often use stylish text to make their profiles,
      usernames, captions, and messages more distinctive.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
      Social Media Bios
    </h3>

    <p class="mb-5">
      You can create stylish text for Instagram, TikTok, Facebook, X,
      and other social platforms. A decorative font can make a short bio
      or profile description stand out.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
      Usernames and Display Names
    </h3>

    <p class="mb-5">
      Gamers and social media users can use different Unicode styles for
      usernames and display names when the platform supports those
      characters.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3">
      Messages and Captions
    </h3>

    <p>
      Stylish text can also be used in messages, comments, captions,
      announcements, and other short pieces of online content.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
      Font Generator vs. Real Fonts
    </h2>

    <p class="mb-4">
      One important thing to understand is that many online "font
      generators" do not actually change the font of a webpage or install
      a new font on your device.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-4">
      Instead, Unicode-based generators replace ordinary characters with
      other Unicode characters that have different visual appearances.
      This is why the generated result can often be copied and pasted into
      places where normal font formatting is not available.
    </p>

    <p>
      However, compatibility can vary. Some uncommon Unicode characters
      may not display correctly on older devices or applications.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
      Why Use an Online Font Generator?
    </h2>

    <div class="space-y-5">

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">
          Easy to Use
        </h3>
        <p>
          You do not need graphic design experience. Type your text,
          select a style, and copy the result.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">
          No Font Installation
        </h3>
        <p>
          Unicode-based text generators do not require you to download
          and install a traditional font file before creating stylish text.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">
          Quick Copy and Paste
        </h3>
        <p>
          Once your text has been generated, you can copy your preferred
          style and paste it wherever the characters are supported.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">
          Useful for Social Media
        </h3>
        <p>
          Fancy text can be useful for bios, captions, usernames, comments,
          and other creative social media content.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
      How to Choose the Right Font Style
    </h2>

    <p class="mb-4">
      The best font style depends on where you plan to use the text.
      For professional content, a simple bold or italic style may be
      easier to read. For a gaming username or creative profile, you may
      prefer gothic, bubble, cursive, or decorative styles.
    </p>

    <p>
      Try several styles before choosing one. Readability is usually more
      important than using the most complicated design.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
      Frequently Asked Questions
    </h2>

    <div class="space-y-6">

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">
          Is a font generator free?
        </h3>
        <p>
          Many online font generators are available for free. You can
          generate stylish text without purchasing a traditional font.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">
          Can I copy and paste generated fonts?
        </h3>
        <p>
          Yes. Unicode-based font generators create text characters that
          can usually be copied and pasted into apps and websites that
          support those Unicode characters.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">
          Do font generators work on Instagram?
        </h3>
        <p>
          Many Unicode text styles can be pasted into Instagram bios,
          captions, comments, and other supported text fields. However,
          compatibility can vary depending on the characters and platform.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">
          Are these real font files?
        </h3>
        <p>
          Usually not. A Unicode font generator generally creates styled
          Unicode characters rather than generating or installing a
          traditional font file.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2">
          Can I use fancy fonts for my username?
        </h3>
        <p>
          Yes, if the platform supports the Unicode characters used by
          the style. Always check how the username appears before using it.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
      Create Your Stylish Text
    </h2>

    <p class="mb-4">
      Ready to try different font styles? Enter your text into our free
      font generator and explore different options for your bio, username,
      caption, or message.
    </p>

    <a
      href="/"
      class="inline-flex items-center font-semibold text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 underline"
    >
      Try the Font Generator
    </a>
  </section>

</article>

<FaqSection lang={lang} />
  <SchemaOrg lang={lang} pageUrl={pageUrl} siteUrl={siteUrl + base} logoUrl={logoUrl} />
</BaseLayout>
